    "title": "New York State Police presence in Southport Wednesday night - NewsBreak",
    "text": "SOUTHPORT, N.Y. ( WETM ) — A police presence was outside of a home in Southport on Wednesday night. According to an 18 News reporter at the scene, an investigator, along with New York State Police, responded to a home located on the corner of Cypress and Cedar Street in Southport sometime after 7 p.m. on Wednesday, July 30. More specifically, state police were outside the home located at 705 Cedar Street, the reporter explained. This is a developing story, and 18 News will provide updates as more information becomes available. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WETM - MyTwinTiers.com.",
